-- Rollback: The Roles of the Wife: A Biblical Perspective (9286b7e0)
UPDATE public.profiles
SET gospel_data = '[{"title":"The Roles of the Wife: A Biblical Perspective","linkUrl":"https://crosspointechurchmn.snappages.site/media/tdmq4fy/roles-of-the-wife","section":"1","subsections":[{"title":"Introduction","content":"","questions":[],"nestedSubsections":[{"title":"The Primary Role of the Wife is to be a Helper.","content":"<p>Genesis 2:18 Then the LORD God said, “It is not good for the man to be alone; I will make him a helper suitable for him.”</p><ol><li><p>Martha Peace states, “The order of creation has significance in the role of the husband and the wife. The husband was created to rule over the earth; the wife, later, was created to be a ‘helper’ that would be suitable for him.”<sup>1</sup> <br>Matthew 20:25-28 But Jesus called them to Himself and said, “You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their great men exercise authority over them. It is not this way among you, but whoever wishes to become great among you shall be your servant, and whoever wishes to be first among you shall be your slave; just as the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life a ransom for many.”</p></li><li><p>Jesus is the head of the church. He is our Lord, and yet He does not lord it over us. He came into this world, not to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many. <br>1 Corinthians 11:7-9 For a man ought to have his head covered, since he is the image and glory of God; but the woman is the glory of man. For man does not originate from woman, but woman from man; for indeed man was not created for the woman’s sake, but woman for the man’s sake.</p></li><li><p>As the husband’s helper, the wife’s God-given roles are to love, submit, and revere her husband.</p></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"The Role of the Wife is to be a Lover.","content":"<p>Titus 2:4 These older women must train the younger women to love their husbands and their children,</p><ol><li><p>The state of a marriage can degenerate to the point where a wife will say that she no longer ‘loves’ her husband.</p><ol><li><p>When a wife loses her love for her husband, she has lost the feeling of being ‘in love’ with her husband, and it was not biblical love in the first place.</p><ol><li><p>Biblical love is an act or determination of the will. Biblical love is not a feeling which comes and goes freely.</p></li><li><p>The misconceptions about biblical love have always been a problem, which is why the Bible says a wife needs to be ‘trained’ to love her husband. She needs to be taught what biblical love really is.</p></li><li><p>Jay Adams states, “Love is not feeling first. Before all else it is the determination to do good for another person because God has told you to do so. Love begins, therefore, with a desire to please God. Love toward another is a willingness to give to him whatever you have that he needs, because you know that God wants you to. Where true love exists, the feeling follows soon enough.”<em><sup>2</sup></em></p></li></ol></li><li><p>God calls a Christian wife to a ‘giving love.’ She is to be concerned more about giving herself to her husband, rather than getting something from him.</p><ol><li><p>Biblical love “is not feeling and desire; it is not something over which one has no control.”<sup>3</sup> Biblical love is material and tangible; it can be seen.</p><ol><li><p>Jesus Christ demonstrated this tangible love when He washed the disciple’s feet. <br>John 13:5 After that, he poured water into a basin and began to wash his disciples’ feet, drying them with the towel that was wrapped around him.</p></li><li><p>Jesus Christ demonstrated this tangible love when He gave himself up for the church. <br>Ephesians 5:25 Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ also loved the church and gave Himself up for her,</p></li><li><p>God the Father showed this tangible love when He gave His only Son to the world. <br>John 3:16 For God so loved the world, that He gave His only begotten Son, that whoever believes in Him shall not perish, but have eternal life.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>Biblical love “is not first a feeling, but a rather a giving of oneself.”<sup>4</sup></p></li><li><p>When a wife loves her husband in a biblical manner, she is not conjuring up ‘feelings’ for her husband, but rather she is giving to him and serving him.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>Since biblical love is tangible and concrete, it can be learned and practiced.<sup>5</sup> <br>Titus 2:4 These older women must train the younger women to love their husbands and their children,</p><ol><li><p>Wives are called to love their husbands biblically. If you do not have feelings toward your husband, you must love him anyway. Biblical love is an act of the will.</p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Word of Caution:</strong> It is easy to live by feelings. It is harder to live by biblical principles. If a wife’s feelings toward her husband have become bitter, she must not let those feelings rule her! <br>Luke 9:23 And He was saying to them all, “If anyone wishes to come after Me, he must deny himself, and take up his cross daily and follow me.</p><ol><li><p>Feelings are good indicators, telling us when something is wrong, such as the check engine light on the dashboard of your car.</p></li><li><p>A wife that has negative feelings toward her husband needs to confess this as sin, repent, work to get things right with him and God, and begin to concretely and tangibly love her husband.</p><ol><li><p>If you do not love him, how can you be his helper? How can you fulfill the mandate of your calling from God?</p></li><li><p>Biblical love is an act of the will, a determination to do good to another because God has told you to do so. When you do this, the feelings will follow soon enough!<sup>6</sup></p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"The Role of the Wife is to Submit to her Husband.","content":"<p>Ephesians 5:22 Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.</p><ol><li><p>Martha Peace states, “Submission to her husband is the heart of God for the Christians wife” (emphasis hers).<sup>7</sup> <br>Ephesians 5:15-17 Therefore be careful how you walk, not as unwise men but as wise, making the most of your time, because the days are evil. So then do not be foolish, but understand what the will of the Lord is.</p><ol><li><p>God has called wives to place themselves under the authority of their husband. <br>Ephesians 5:24 But as the church is subject to Christ, so also the wives ought to be to their husbands in everything.</p><ol><li><p>When a wife places herself under the authority of her husband, it does not make a wife inferior to their husbands in any way. <br>Galatians 3:28 There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither slave nor free man, there is neither male nor female; for you are all one in Christ Jesus.</p></li><li><p>Jesus Christ is not inferior to the Father, and yet He submits Himself to the Father in all things. <br>Philippians 2:5-8 Have this attitude in yourselves which was also in Christ Jesus, who, although He existed in the form og God, did not regard equality with God a thing to be grasped, but emptied Himself, taking the form of a bond-servant, and being made in the likeness of men. Being found in appearance as a man, He humbled Himself by becoming obedient to the point of death, even death on a cross. <br>John 5:30 I can do nothing on My own initiative. As I hear, I judge; and My judgment is just, because I do not seek My own will, but the will of Him who sent Me.</p><ol><li><p>Wives are not inferior because they have been called to submission. Jesus Christ always submitted to the Father, yet He is fully God and equal to the Father.</p></li></ol></li></ol></li><li><p>Wives are called to a broad scope of submission.</p><ol><li><p>The church provides “the pattern for the wife’s submission to her husband.”<sup>8</sup> She is to submit to her husband “in everything,” just as the church is submit to Christ in everything. <br>Ephesians 5:24 But as the church is subject to Christ, so also the wives ought to be to their husbands in everything.</p></li><li><p>The ‘everything’ would include such things as “finances, decorating the house, the length of her hair, what to have for supper, and the discipline of the children.”<sup>9</sup></p></li><li><p>‘Everything’ does not include sin. <br>Acts 5:29 But Peter and the apostles answered, “We must obey God rather than men.”</p></li></ol></li><li><p>The manner in which a wife submits is essential. <br>Ephesians 5:22 Wives, be subject to your own husbands, as to the Lord.</p><ol><li><p>A wife is not merely called to submit to her husband; she is called to submit to him as to the Lord! This should be done with a willing and joyful spirit.</p></li><li><p>A Christian wife should see submitting to her husband as an opportunity to serve and please God 2 Corinthians 5:9.</p></li><li><p>When a wife refuses to submit to her husband, she should consider if she would display this same attitude toward Jesus Christ! <br>Psalms 100:2 Serve the LORD with gladness; Come before Him with joyful singing.</p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Word of Caution: </strong>Our modern society views submission as negative, becoming very unpopular. The idea of a wife submitting to her husband sounds oppressive. This view is even rejected among many ‘Christians!’</p><ol><li><p>We must understand that the idea of Christian wives submitting to their husbands is from God’s Word, not man’s ideas. Philippians 2:3-4 Do nothing from selfishness or empty conceit, but with humility of mind regard one another as more important than yourselves; do not merely look out for your own personal interests, but also for the interests of others.</p></li><li><p>Christians are called to submit in various ways. Such as:</p><ol><li><p>To your elders. <br>1 Peter 5:5 You younger men, likewise, be subject to your elders; and all of you, clothe yourselves with humility toward one another, for God is opposed to the proud, but give grace to the humble.</p></li><li><p>To your governing authorities. <br>Romans 13:1 Every person is to be in subjection to the governing authorities. For there is no authority except from God, and those which exist are established by God.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>All believers are to have a submissive attitude. <br>John 14:21 He who has My commandments and keeps them is the one who loves Me; and he who love Me will be loved by My Father, and I will love him and will disclose Myself to him.</p></li><li><p>It is dishonorable when a wife fails to submit to her husband. <br>Titus 2:3-5 Older women likewise are to be reverent in their behavior, not malicious gossips nor enslaved to much wine, teaching what is good, so that they may encourage the young women to love their husbands, to love their children, to be sensible, pure, workers at home, kind, being subject to their own husbands, so that the word of God will not be dishonored. <br>Romans 12:2 And do not be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what the will of God is, that which is good and acceptable and perfect.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>It is a high calling to submit yourself under another person’s authority. <br>1 Peter 3:1-6 In the same way, you wives, be submissive to your own husbands so that even if any of them are disobedient to the word, they may be won without a word by the behavior of their wives, as they observe your chaste and respectful behavior. Your adornment must not be merely external—braiding the hair, and wearing gold jewelry, or putting on dresses; but let it be the hidden person of the heart, with the imperishable quality of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is precious in the sight of God. For in this way in former times the holy women also, who hoped in God, used to adorn themselves, being submissive to their own husbands; just as Sarah obeyed Abraham, calling him Lord, and you have become her children if you do what is right without being frightened by any fear.</p><ol><li><p>Martha Peace states, “Submitting will not always be fun, but there is always joy in glorifying the Lord Jesus Christ. You should therefore commit yourself to learning submission, not with a dread of what is to come, but with an anticipation of how you can best glorify your Lord.”<sup>10</sup></p></li></ol></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"The Role of the Wife is to Revere her Husband.","content":"<p>Ephesians 5:33 Nevertheless, each individual among you also is to love his own wife even as himself, and the wife must see to it that she respects her husband.</p><ol><li><p>The Amplified Bible says, “. . . let the wife see that she respects and reverences her husband—that she notices him, regards him, honors him, prefers him, venerates and esteems him, and that she defers to him, praises him, and loves and admires him exceedingly.”</p></li><li><p>To reverence someone is to show them “deep respect tinged with awe, or veneration.”<sup>11</sup></p><ol><li><p><strong>Word of Caution:</strong> The idea of reverencing your husband “runs counter to our culture.”<sup>12</sup> It certainly clashes with today’s feminist movement, yet the wife has been called to this role. It is both a moral command and a means of glorifying God.</p></li></ol></li><li><p>A Christian wife must reverence her husband as an act of the will.</p><ol><li><p>If a husband is unworthy of reverence, his wife is still to reverence him simply because of the office he is in; he is the ‘head of the wife” Ephesians 5:23.</p></li></ol></li></ol>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]},{"title":"Practical Ways a Wife can be her Husband’s Helper.","content":"<ol><li><p>Make your home a place of encouragement and comfort. Make sure there is an attitude of love, warmth, and respect in the home at all times.</p></li><li><p>Be dependable and trustworthy.</p></li><li><p>Have a gentle and cheerful attitude.</p></li><li><p>Be content and grateful.</p></li><li><p>Be patient and forgiving.</p></li><li><p>Listen to him; show an interest in his concerns.</p></li><li><p>Be industrious, frugal, and ambitious.</p></li><li><p>When correcting your husband, always be gentle and respectful.</p></li><li><p>Keep yourself beautiful, especially in the inner person.</p></li><li><p>Walk closely to the Lord, keep growing in Christ.</p></li></ol><p></p><p></p><ol><li><p>1Martha Peace, The Excellent Wife: A Biblical Perspective, 49.</p></li><li><p>Jay E. Adams, What Do You Do When Your Marriage Goes Sour?, 1-2.</p></li><li><p>Jay E. Adams, Christian Counselor’s Manual, 151.</p></li><li><p>Jay E. Adams, Christian Counselor’s Manual, 151.</p></li><li><p>Jay E. Adams, Christian Counselor’s Manual, 153.</p></li><li><p>Jay E. Adams, What Do You Do When Your Marriage Goes Sour?, 1-2.</p></li><li><p>Martha Peace, The Excellent Wife: A Biblical Perspective, 129.</p></li><li><p>F. F. Bruce, The Epistles to the Colossians, to Philemon, and to the Ephesians, The New International Commentary on the New Testament, 386.</p></li><li><p>Martha Peace, The Excellent Wife: A Biblical Perspective, 140.</p></li><li><p>Martha Peace, The Excellent Wife: A Biblical Perspective, 134.</p></li><li><p>Emery and Brewster, The New Century Dictionary, s.v. “reverence.”</p></li><li><p>James Montgomery Boice, Ephesians: An Expositional Commentary, 195.</p></li></ol><p></p>","questions":[],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"scriptureReferences":[]}],"linkDescription":"Watch the recording of this content."},{"title":"Homework","section":"2","subsections":[{"title":"Homework Questions","content":"<p>Complete the exercises below and save your answers.</p>","questions":[{"id":"q-1762815699165-cmazjtvcl","question":"<p>Memory Verse: </p><p>Ephesians 5:22 Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:01:39.165Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815727530-636ay6o5j","question":"<p>Scripture: Wives, read Ephesians 5:22-33 with your husband. <br>Discuss with your husband what it means to “submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord”</p><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:07.530Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815743329-368lco85v","question":"<p>Review and discuss this lesson with your spouse.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:23.329Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815771780-km1fv8sxs","question":"<p>Pray daily for God’s help to love, revere, and submit to your husband “as unto the Lord.”</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:02:51.780Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815788546-a7zpmi1z2","question":"<p>Attend Church together.</p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:03:08.546Z","maxLength":2000},{"id":"q-1762815849312-qrorii0ba","question":"<p>Application</p><ul><li><p>Make a list of ways that you have shown disrespect to your husband. Confess it to him and to God and ask for forgiveness. Put this disrespectful behavior “off.” </p></li><li><p>Make a list of 10 things you respect about your husband. Tell him! </p></li><li><p>Make a list of 10 ways you can respect him by how you live, start living it out! </p></li><li><p>Make a list of 10 ways that you submit to your husband “as unto the Lord.” Start doing it right away!</p></li></ul><p></p>","createdAt":"2025-11-10T23:04:09.312Z","maxLength":2000}],"nestedSubsections":[]}]}]'::jsonb, updated_at = NOW()
WHERE slug = '9286b7e0';
